{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character","id":948011,"title":"My questionable vampire character...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T13:39:09-07:00","id":948011,"title":"My questionable vampire character...","content":"So i'm going to be playing VtR for the first time, and my character is a bit of a special snow flake. He is a 16 boy that was embraced as a Nosferatu. His beginning disciplines are 2 dots in Protean, and 1 dot in Vigor, which I plan to keep pushing up with experience throughout the game. The idea is that this is a fairly gentle kid, that was vamped against his will, and now lives like a runaway teen, with no sire (Storyteller decision, since we are all naturally embraced by some freak accident) unwilling to hurt people, except for other vampires when necessary to protect others/himself. Ultimately I plan for him to find a cause or other Kindred that he can believe in, and be an assassin/enforcer that is strong enough to kill other vampires, but not rely on Childer, or Ghouls for his personal strength There are two questionable things I am doing with this character.<br /> <br /> First of all, my plan is to find a slaughter house, and use the first dot of Protean Unmarked Grave, to feed from the blood that is spilled into the drain above. This is his way of satisfying his need for vitae, without hurting anyone. I suggested that the Storyteller might have the mafia throw in a body to create some drama, so I'm not really trying to get around the conflict in the game, but I can see how some might see this as meta-gaming.<br /> <br /> Second, and probably the most questionable is the use of my Predatory Aspects for Protean. I plan on getting Prehensile Tail, and express it as 2 shapechanging tentecals that emerge from my lower back, kind of like in the darkness games <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lS0cBuSZBTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lS0cBuSZBTM</a>, or Tokyo ghoul. <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=tokyo+ghoul+kagune&amp;espv=2&amp;biw=1366&amp;bih=643&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi_3-K-2LfOAhUGPCYKHd9UDK0Q_AUIBigB#imgrc=z1R_uoVS_BPIrM%3A\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=toky..._uoVS_BPIrM%3A</a><br /> <br /> I want to us the Predatory Aspect Claws so it can be used to attack at a distance with lamprey-like mouths <a href=\"http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7078/7129322663_7861d71fca_z.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7078/7...61d71fca_z.jpg</a> . I also want to get the Predatory Aspect Wall Crawling, which when combined with my Vigor, can let me justify doing the spiderman thing and use the tenticals to swing from roof tops. I don't know how many storytellers would allow this, but I figure that if can grab them from a distance with the prehensile tail in a grapple, could use my vampire bite this way and feed from a distance with the mouths on my tenticals?<br /> <br /> Am I being too creative here guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-10-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:17:48-07:00","id":948057,"title":"","content":"I take it there's already some house ruling going on, with a Nosferatu starting with Protean 2, Vigor 1. You usually have to start with at least 2 dots of in-clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> As for your ideas of how to use your Predatory Aspects, I think getting Prehensile Tail and narrating it as tentacles is fine. Tentacles are a thing actual predatory animals have, so there's no issue with having them, and using the Prehensile Tail mechanics to represent it. Taking Wall Crawling and using your tentacles as extra limbs for that purpose also seems reasonable to me. But, claws and/or mouths at the ends of the tentacles is beyond the scope of Predatory Aspect. That's distinctly an Unnatural Aspect if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Living in a slaughterhouse and using Unmarked Grave to feed seems like a fine justification to allow you to purchase up to 5 dots in Herd. Assuming the character's blood potency is low enough to survive on animals without having to spend Willpower, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:28:16-07:00","id":948067,"title":"","content":"It's a more high-action or gonzo style concept than what I usually go for. Here's my thoughts:<ul><li>By RAW You can only start with one Out-of-Clan discipline out of your free-three, so going with (2) Protean at jump is normally impossible unless you're Clan Gangel or through earned experience.</li> <li>No-Sire / Freak-Accident is tough to pull off in a non-cliche way. But it sounds ST driven, so hopefully it gets some meat in the metaplot.</li> <li>Not relying on other NPCs is a red-flag in terms of avoiding conflict. Be careful that you aren't trying to create a 'drama-free' life for this kid so they don't have anything to lose. Who's his Touchstone? If you're planning on a place or item, I'd see that as another step along that potentially concerning path of the loner-assassin archetype.</li> <li>Slaughterhouse should be no sweat. No tougher than animal hunting, really, just a creative way to do so.</li> <li>For the prehensile tail, some might pause in terms of - what is the actual animal being formed into for this? But - if it's just a cosmetic thing, there's no real harm - unless you're trying to expand the two tentacles into <b>two</b> extra 'hands' instead of the normal one.</li> <li>Wall Crawling is already good to go with Predatory Aspect.</li> <li>Rooftop Swinging is a little more difficult, but reskinning Patagia should do the trick. Just keep in mind the limitation of Patagia. If you want full aerial mobility, you'd need to reskin Flight, which would be Unnatural Aspect (Prot 4)</li> <li>The Lamprey Mouths for distance feeding as a Claws reskin I'd flat out deny. I <i>might</i> be convinced to come up with a reskin for Horrid Talons (Prot 4) - but I'd drop the other stats to compensate. Probably drop the Armor Piercing Trait and maybe lower the Bonus from (+2) to (+1) as well.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:02:08-07:00","id":948087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948057#post948057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it there's already some house ruling going on, with a Nosferatu starting with Protean 2, Vigor 1. You usually have to start with at least 2 dots of in-clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> As for your ideas of how to use your Predatory Aspects, I think getting Prehensile Tail and narrating it as tentacles is fine. Tentacles are a thing actual predatory animals have, so there's no issue with having them, and using the Prehensile Tail mechanics to represent it. Taking Wall Crawling and using your tentacles as extra limbs for that purpose also seems reasonable to me. But, claws and/or mouths at the ends of the tentacles is beyond the scope of Predatory Aspect. That's distinctly an Unnatural Aspect if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Living in a slaughterhouse and using Unmarked Grave to feed seems like a fine justification to allow you to purchase up to 5 dots in Herd. Assuming the character's blood potency is low enough to survive on animals without having to spend Willpower, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, you can take out of clan disciplines during character creation. Beyond Character creation it cost 4 exp instead of 3. And I think at least one dot has to be a clan discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:16:45-07:00","id":948102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948087#post948087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, you can take out of clan disciplines during character creation. Beyond Character creation it cost 4 exp instead of 3. And I think at least one dot has to be a clan discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see page 81 &quot;Choose three dots in Disiplines. At least two must be from the vampire's in-clan Disiplines.&quot;<br /> Also as a clan exclusive discipline you would need to learn it from someone who knew it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:19:28-07:00","id":948106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948067#post948067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a more high-action or gonzo style concept than what I usually go for. Here's my thoughts:<ul><li>By RAW You can only start with one Out-of-Clan discipline out of your free-three, so going with (2) Protean at jump is normally impossible unless you're Clan Gangel or through earned experience.</li> <li>No-Sire / Freak-Accident is tough to pull off in a non-cliche way. But it sounds ST driven, so hopefully it gets some meat in the metaplot.</li> <li>Not relying on other NPCs is a red-flag in terms of avoiding conflict. Be careful that you aren't trying to create a 'drama-free' life for this kid so they don't have anything to lose. Who's his Touchstone? If you're planning on a place or item, I'd see that as another step along that potentially concerning path of the loner-assassin archetype.</li> <li>Slaughterhouse should be no sweat. No tougher than animal hunting, really, just a creative way to do so.</li> <li>For the prehensile tail, some might pause in terms of - what is the actual animal being formed into for this? But - if it's just a cosmetic thing, there's no real harm - unless you're trying to expand the two tentacles into <b>two</b> extra 'hands' instead of the normal one.</li> <li>Wall Crawling is already good to go with Predatory Aspect.</li> <li>Rooftop Swinging is a little more difficult, but reskinning Patagia should do the trick. Just keep in mind the limitation of Patagia. If you want full aerial mobility, you'd need to reskin Flight, which would be Unnatural Aspect (Prot 4)</li> <li>The Lamprey Mouths for distance feeding as a Claws reskin I'd flat out deny. I <i>might</i> be convinced to come up with a reskin for Horrid Talons (Prot 4) - but I'd drop the other stats to compensate. Probably drop the Armor Piercing Trait and maybe lower the Bonus from (+2) to (+1) as well.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I made this character specifically to be a trauma magnet. He is sensitive, and will seek out attachments with other vampires. His sister (touchstone) lives in a mental hospital with a rare form of autism and no grasp of human morality. He loves his sister and wants her to understand how to function socially. I'm trying to get the story teller to make her turn out as a beast later on. <br /> <br /> maybe I could change my claw predatory aspect into a mouth that does no damage? It could still need a grapple first, unless I'm in frenzy.<br /> <br /> As for the storyteller, he has made the best game I have every played. I suspect the source of our embrace is caused by a Strix ritual, since he mentioned its happened world wide and the Kindred are straining to maintain the masquerade. Our characters all start out dead, and wakeup in our graves, more, ect. Really looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-10-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:39:59-07:00","id":948128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948102#post948102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, see page 81 &amp;quot;Choose three dots in Disiplines. At least two must be from the vampire's in-clan Disiplines.&amp;quot;<br /> Also as a clan exclusive discipline you would need to learn it from someone who knew it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I guess I'll have to put 2 in vigor then. I can buy the tenticals later at a story appropriate time when my character is forced to fight. My Storyteller told me physical disciplines don't need a teacher, but I'm not sure If that applies to Protean or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:59:00-07:00","id":948148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948128#post948128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I guess I'll have to put 2 in vigor then. I can buy the tenticals later at a story appropriate time when my character is forced to fight. My Storyteller told me physical disciplines don't need a teacher, but I'm not sure If that applies to Protean or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean is &quot;THE&quot; Gangrel clan-specific discipline and requires you to drink the blood of someone who knows Protean to learn it as a non-Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:44:37-07:00","id":948170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948128#post948128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I guess I'll have to put 2 in vigor then. I can buy the tenticals later at a story appropriate time when my character is forced to fight. My Storyteller told me physical disciplines don't need a teacher, but I'm not sure If that applies to Protean or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean isn't a physical Discipline. The physical Disciplines are Celerity, Resilience, and Vigor. And while they don't require a teacher, they do still count as out-of-clan for the purposes of exp costs and character creation restrictions. Vigor 2 Protean 1 works for a Nosferatu, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:58:27-07:00","id":948175,"title":"","content":"Why not go Gangrel instead of Nosferatu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:11:56-07:00","id":948177,"title":"","content":"I love the nosferatu clan bane. My character is one of the black eyed kids of urban legend. Also, if I did that Vigor would cost more each level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:41:13-07:00","id":948233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948177#post948177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the nosferatu clan bane. My character is one of the black eyed kids of urban legend. Also, if I did that Vigor would cost more each level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean is going to cost more now too. like crimson owl said, you will have to have Imbibed blood from someone who knew protean in order for you to know it. <br /> <br /> Either way one of your two favored disciplines is going to be out of clan.<br /> <br /> While nos is my second favorite clan, from experience in running groups, they are hardest to create and play. The haunt seems to be a hard concept for beginning players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:30:45-07:00","id":948273,"title":"","content":"Starting with Protean 1 is fine. The tentacles thing I wouldn't allow because it deviates too far from the root of the power, that is animal shapechanging. A Nightmare + Protean devotion? <i>Maybe</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:38:51-07:00","id":948312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948273#post948273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting with Protean 1 is fine. The tentacles thing I wouldn't allow because it deviates too far from the root of the power, that is animal shapechanging. A Nightmare + Protean devotion? <i>Maybe</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it deviate? They are basically just lampreys that grow out of his back. Lampreys are animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:43:17-07:00","id":948317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948233#post948233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Protean is going to cost more now too. like crimson owl said, you will have to have Imbibed blood from someone who knew protean in order for you to know it. <br /> <br /> Either way one of your two favored disciplines is going to be out of clan.<br /> <br /> While nos is my second favorite clan, from experience in running groups, they are hardest to create and play. The haunt seems to be a hard concept for beginning players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you need to imbibe blood to level a discipline if you already started paying for it in character creation do you? It will only cost me 4 exp to get it to 2 dots. After that I'm just gonna pump vigor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:27:19-07:00","id":948380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948312#post948312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does it deviate? They are basically just lampreys that grow out of his back. Lampreys are animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean doesn't allow for entire animals to be attached to you that can do their own attacks. ( besides 3 which turns you into an animal ). Protean 2 and 4 only allows your body to transform bits of itself into a piece of an animal. Claws, fangs, wings, tails. Only parts. If you wanted tentacles, make it function like a tail. But personally I wouldn't allow an entire lamprey to be attached to you and wiggling. Nor would I allow you to feed through your tentacle through protean 2. With a devotion or something, yes. Maybe transform your mouth into theirs... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948317#post948317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you need to imbibe blood to level a discipline if you already started paying for it in character creation do you? It will only cost me 4 exp to get it to 2 dots. After that I'm just gonna pump vigor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon creation you still need to follow the discipline rules. To learn a clan specific discipline ( which protean is Gangrel's) you have to imbibe the vitae of a vampire who knows it. <br /> <br /> Since you were spontaneously created you can't even say &quot;well my sire knew it&quot;<br /> <br /> It would be a call for your story teller, personally I would not allow it upon creation without it worked into your backstory as it completely negates the possible negatives ( addiction and bond ) gaining something really big for nothing. <br /> <br /> See the other thread about clans sharing personal disciplines.<br /> <br /> Another example. You couldn't just know blood sorcery or coils upon creation just because they can be the 1 out of clan choice. You would still need to back it up with all the other requirements. <br /> <br /> What is your Nos's Haunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-11-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:38:00-07:00","id":948444,"title":"","content":"I think the Lampreys are perfectly fine as an Unnatural Aspect. That to me is basically the animal-feature-turned-nightmare-fuel level of the discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:24:44-07:00","id":948587,"title":"","content":"I don't know if your ST will go for it but you could ask about starting with a Bloodline, in Bloodlines the Chosen there was a line of caniballistic (on my phone, can't get the right spelling) Nos who had a unique discipline that may as well be the 2e Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:21:46-07:00","id":948622,"title":"","content":"I'll look into it. He seems to pretty much like much like my take on things though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:26:19-07:00","id":948626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948587#post948587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if your ST will go for it but you could ask about starting with a Bloodline, in Bloodlines the Chosen there was a line of caniballistic (on my phone, can't get the right spelling) Nos who had a unique discipline that may as well be the 2e Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have Bloodlines the Chosen, but I don't see a disipline, or bloodline called Nos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:32:04-07:00","id":948628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948626#post948626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have Bloodlines the Chosen, but I don't see a disipline, or bloodline called Nos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nos is short for Nosferatu, Live Bait is referring to Noctuku, a cannibalistic Nosferatu bloodline with a Protean-like Bloodline Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:58:17-07:00","id":951379,"title":"","content":"It might be my bias, but for physical disciplines that don't get new powers per dot, I've always preferred to go broad instead of focused. Vigor 1 + Celerity 1 seems much more effective than naked Vigor 3. That's my personal feeling on deciding to pump Vigor in general + wanting to be a combat monster. My gut instinct is that you would be better served with splitting your disciplines instead of heavy investing into Vigor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:05:59-07:00","id":951588,"title":"","content":"I dont think you need to follow the mentoring rules for starting eith another clans signature discipline. The teaching rules are from teaching. Starting disciplines are things you just have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:40:09-07:00","id":951602,"title":"","content":"As for physical disciplines, the Celerity isnt linear. The first dot is worth far more, because it opens up the ability to move instantly, the ability to pre empt actions, and the ability to cheat initiative. Further dots just allow you to do those things more often and more reliably while also increasing defense.<br /> <br /> So the first dot of Celerity is extremely important, and I would argue it is the &quot;best&quot; physical discipline if you are only getting one dot. If youbare getting multiple dots, you still probably want one of then to be Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:17:29-07:00","id":951682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951588#post951588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think you need to follow the mentoring rules for starting eith another clans signature discipline. The teaching rules are from teaching. Starting disciplines are things you just have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the storyteller actually. I know more than one ST who has a character's sire teach them (or arrange for them to be taught) any starting disciplines that aren't physical. A sire can't teach a power they don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:20:13-07:00","id":951686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951682#post951682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on the storyteller actually. I know more than one ST who has a character's sire teach them (or arrange for them to be taught) any starting disciplines that aren't physical. A sire can't teach a power they don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree with this. As with the bonus 3 merits and Humanity at 7 the starting things are often things obtained between the embrace and the moment of the chronicle. That's why one of the three can be a Sorcery, which can only be taught by others. <br /> If a vampire would gain three disciplines as things &quot;you just have&quot;, then nobody would be able to start with a Sorcery, and yet, that is possible. So at least in my game, any starting non in-clan disciplines must be explained. Sometime's it's &quot;I've joined this covenant and they taught me&quot;, other times it's &quot;my sire taught me&quot;, which then pulls in the teaching/learning rules and the blood drinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:30:26-07:00","id":951692,"title":"","content":"The right answer to the &quot;can you or can not learn on your own&quot; conundrum is simple - it depends on the Chronicle (as trite as it sounds). That's because &quot;how you learn Disciplines&quot; is an important Setting Lever that can be set in multiple positions, and each of these positions can be used to construct setting in a different way, and thus - emphasize different themes and provide different gameplay patterns and features, which results in a unique roleplaying experience.<br /> Very basic example: if you want a game that emphasizes hierarchy, dependency on others and moving inside (or against) the chains of local society, you might set the lever to a value of &quot;needs teachers&quot;, simply to make Kindreds need each other and introduce additional trading good to the market.<br /> If you want to focus on more personal game, where each Kindred is more of an island and where hierarchy is less important than individual motivations and agendas (this is a very characteristic type of supernatural stories where you could say that each supernatural individual is their own &quot;player&quot;), you might put it to a value of &quot;may develop freely&quot;, because it deemphasizes the mentoring and trading in exchange for more space that can be used on personal growth and characterization.l<br /> <br /> There is no single fit all-size answer.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And in game-text, it's solved by saying that new Disciplines can manifest on their own, while deliberate &quot;learning&quot; can be done by stalking other Vampires. Which gives GM a choice of saying either &quot;yeah, you have XP for this, you spent it and it decided to manifest&quot; or &quot;nah, go find a teacher&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-16-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:32:20-07:00","id":951732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951686#post951686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agree with this. As with the bonus 3 merits and Humanity at 7 the starting things are often things obtained between the embrace and the moment of the chronicle. That's why one of the three can be a Sorcery, which can only be taught by others.<br /> If a vampire would gain three disciplines as things &quot;you just have&quot;, then nobody would be able to start with a Sorcery, and yet, that is possible. So at least in my game, any starting non in-clan disciplines must be explained. Sometime's it's &quot;I've joined this covenant and they taught me&quot;, other times it's &quot;my sire taught me&quot;, which then pulls in the teaching/learning rules and the blood drinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you here. When there are clear rules like the one below, I do not think it's possible for a Nosferatu to just start with protean just because they were &quot;born&quot; with it. Character creation is not a time where you get to bend the rules. Otherwise why not just take a bunch of merits you dont meet the prerequisites for just because you were born with it? Like Why not have your Nosferatu have Kiss of the Succubus, Or be Born with Producer?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you bend the rule for 1 thing, why not all of them? The book says sometimes disciplines just manifest which is true, but then it goes further to say additional rules for UNIQUE CLAN Disciplines. Protean, Dominate, Nightmare, Auspex, Majesty are unique to a specific clan. so I dont think they just manifest ( unless of course you have it in your background your sire had these things, then.. problem solved ) The way I have always played it, is you can randomly manifest anything that is not clan specific.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951588#post951588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think you need to follow the mentoring rules for starting eith another clans signature discipline. The teaching rules are from teaching. Starting disciplines are things you just have.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;To learn another clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To learn.. not to be taught. but to put a dot on your paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-16-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:21:53-07:00","id":951914,"title":"","content":"You dont learn things that are innate. That said, sorcery is a valid point. Its furmly in the realm of STs call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:42:44-07:00","id":951929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951914#post951914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You dont learn things that are innate. That said, sorcery is a valid point. Its furmly in the realm of STs call.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in the &quot;Learning Disciplines&quot; section. No where does it say that disciplines are innate and you just poof know them. Disciplines Chapter page 125 right before Animalism.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; Learning Disciplines<br /> Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. <b>To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences. </b>&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> While it is in the story tellers purview to alter this, by RAW you do need to still follow the prerequisites for all disciplines and merits. That just happens to be a prerequisite to learning unique clan disciplines. If any vampire can just manifest Dominate, it takes away from the Ventrue. If any vampire can just suddenly drop into the ground to be safe it takes away from Gangrel. That's not what was intended. There would be no point to having clan specific disciplines of any clan can know any discipline at any time.<br /> <br /> Once you learn it, it is entirely up to the story teller if you need someone to teach you how to use it.. If you just need to sip on someone else's blood and then figure it out on your own or if you need to drink the blood and then be taught by a mentor or sire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, if you can just manifest anything at anytime.. Why not just manifest the 5th dot of everything without building up to it? If they are truly innate, then you shouldn't need the things in between..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-16-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:38:59-07:00","id":951977,"title":"","content":"I've never liked the clan unique disipline rule as it feels artifcial when they can be taken as Bloodline disiplines. Instead I plan to houserule that the first dot in any out of clan disipline requires a teacher or a successful Blood Potency role (you can retry after 11-Humanity nights, ie next night at Humanity 10)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=948628#post948628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nos is short for Nosferatu, Live Bait is referring to Noctuku, a cannibalistic Nosferatu bloodline with a Protean-like Bloodline Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Charlaquin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":".  Used Quote and it wipped the rest of my post, I swear it was better first time but it's hot here. 08-16-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:49:34-07:00","id":951984,"title":"","content":"If I was going to run Vampire again or play in it again, I would request a homerule I always wanted to see in action - Embrace not making you your parent's Clan, and instead your Clan being decided by which Unique Discipline you manifest on your own. But I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:59:33-07:00","id":951998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951977#post951977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never liked the clan unique disipline rule as it feels artifcial when they can be taken as Bloodline disiplines. Instead I plan to houserule that the first dot in any out of clan disipline requires a teacher or a successful Blood Potency role (you can retry after 11-Humanity nights, ie next night at Humanity 10)<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Artificial? the 5 main clans are the whole base of the book? There are tons of clan specific sections and abilities and merits. Do away with any uniqueness... why have banes? Stereotypes? Merits? any of that?<br /> <br /> Anyway you are welcome to Homebrew anything that makes you and your players happy,but we shouldnt confuse people asking for help with Homebrew and RAW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:45:22-07:00","id":952044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951998#post951998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Artificial? the 5 main clans are the whole base of the book? There are tons of clan specific sections and abilities and merits. Do away with any uniqueness... why have banes? Stereotypes? Merits? any of that?<br /> <br /> Anyway you are welcome to Homebrew anything that makes you and your players happy,but we shouldnt confuse people asking for help with Homebrew and RAW</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify it makes the setting feel artificial. The merits and banes are one clan only, the disiplines aren't. As I said above the rule can't be reflecting that it's hard to learn a foreign disipline because other out of clan disiplines don't need a teacher, it can't be because it only comes naturaly to one clan because there's no restrictions on Bloodlines having it so it must be a design decision in universe or out so either the forces that created the first vampires said &quot;ok let's give each type something only they can do&quot; and stuck to it implying a cooperative effort went into making vampires or we acknolage that it's because the people making the game wanted to give each clan its own disipline and tried to enforce this with the rules. In a book that otherwise does a very good job of thinking through how the rules might reflect on the setting this is my way of pruning one of the few things that I don't like.<br /> As for your other point I felt the discussion had drifted towards the nature of what disiplines are, as I said in my reason for edit I forgot that you need to quote before you type anything and I tried to rewite it before anyone read the post so the main reason I posted it wouldn't be missed, I'm sorry if it's not up to standard. Finally it's clearly presented as a house rule so I would hope that would avoid any confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:26:02-07:00","id":952082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952044#post952044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify it makes the setting feel artificial. The merits and banes are one clan only, the disiplines aren't. As I said above the rule can't be reflecting that it's hard to learn a foreign disipline because other out of clan disiplines don't need a teacher, it can't be because it only comes naturaly to one clan because there's no restrictions on Bloodlines having it so it must be a design decision in universe or out so either the forces that created the first vampires said &quot;ok let's give each type something only they can do&quot; and stuck to it implying a cooperative effort went into making vampires or we acknolage that it's because the people making the game wanted to give each clan its own disipline and tried to enforce this with the rules. In a book that otherwise does a very good job of thinking through how the rules might reflect on the setting this is my way of pruning one of the few things that I don't like.<br /> As for your other point I felt the discussion had drifted towards the nature of what disiplines are, as I said in my reason for edit I forgot that you need to quote before you type anything and I tried to rewite it before anyone read the post so the main reason I posted it wouldn't be missed, I'm sorry if it's not up to standard. Finally it's clearly presented as a house rule so I would hope that would avoid any confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodlines have restrictions, which often include being a specific clan and or drinking the blood of the vampire's bloodline which you want to join. Or getting really powerful and creating your own bloodline. There are only 3 2nd E non homebrew bloodlines. so yeah. That's not something that happens everyday.<br /> <br /> Each of the clans is said to come from something else. That's why they are so different and have unique qualities. The vampire who created the daeva and the nos are not the same thing.. Also bloodlines have been created through mutations. They are not the normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:45:57-07:00","id":952098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=951929#post951929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's in the &quot;Learning Disciplines&quot; section. <b>No where does it say that disciplines are innate and you just poof know them.</b> Disciplines Chapter page 125 right before Animalism.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; Learning Disciplines<br /> <b>Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. </b>To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The quote you posted kind of... proves your point wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:59:37-07:00","id":952107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952082#post952082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Bloodlines have restrictions, which often include being a specific clan and or drinking the blood of the vampire's bloodline which you want to join. Or getting really powerful and creating your own bloodline. There are only 3 2nd E non homebrew bloodlines. so yeah. That's not something that happens everyday.<br /> <br /> Each of the clans is said to come from something else. That's why they are so different and have unique qualities. The vampire who created the daeva and the nos are not the same thing.. Also bloodlines have been created through mutations. They are not the normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true but none of that gives an explanation for why clan signature disiplines get their protected status when no other disipline does. As I can not find an in universe expansion I houserule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:59:55-07:00","id":952108,"title":"","content":"Only if you ignore the portion that explicitly says most kindred only display the disciplines of their clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:10:17-07:00","id":952113,"title":"","content":"Then why don't all out of clan disiplines need a teacher like I houserule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:42:35-07:00","id":952166,"title":"","content":"It's kind of indicated in the text, though not stated directly that I know of, that each strain of vampires started out very different from the others. Over time, with the intermingling of blood, they became as similar as they are now. The prime example of this from wherever I first heard this theory is the bonus clan presented in the Tokyo setting in 2e.<br /> <br /> Every Discipline except the Clan ones are common enough that any given vampire's blood might manifest the ability naturally (or, if you like teaching, by trying to force the matter with a teacher).<br /> <br /> Of those, certain Clans manifest certain Disciplines more often than others, perhaps as a reflection of their origins. These are in-clan Disciplines. They're just more common.<br /> <br /> Of these, each Clan has a unique Discipline that originated from their bloodline (in the general sense, not the specific Bloodline sense) which only that Clan manifests naturally. For a vampire of another Clan to manifest this ability, they need some of blood that has already manifested that ability to intermingle with their own. This is because it isn't an ability found in the blood and beast of other clans.<br /> <br /> A Bloodline is what happens when a vampire has blood potent enough that it can start passing on its traits almost like Clan blood can, whatever those traits were be. Based, as one might imagine, upon its founder.<br /> <br /> It's basically magic genetics. Magic because Vampire genetics are passed down by blood, not actual genes, and you can integrate the blood of other vampires into your own magic-blood-genes by ingesting it. Some things (Clan disciplines that are not your own) do not pass down to your Childer unless you create a new bloodline to make your own magic-blood-genes more potent.<br /> <br /> Granted, there's a lot of leaps of logic from the book in that, but it's my interpretation, and it's a good enough way to explain it for those who wanted an explanation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though if you're feeding Vitae to your new Childer to Embrace them, wouldn't they have access to any Out-of-Clan Disciplines in your blood? Maybe! I don't think that's clarified anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 08-16-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:08:20-07:00","id":952183,"title":"","content":"In my opinion? I'd allow it and go for it. Yeah, the bit about having Protean 2 from start is not following RAW, but well, why not? The aspect you've picked is pretty horrifying, certainly, and the Blood twists the Nosferatu in weird ways. I feel the horror potential coming from this child.<br /> <br /> My two cents would be:<br /> <br /> 1) allow the ST to infect your character with a Gangrel Blood Bond (maybe it could have been a fight in the slaughter house the night you arrived, and now the character is claiming that territory. AS a Gangrel, he could well regard you as a threat ... or as a pupil. Besides, his/her Blood would some vampires in you already. If she/he has enemies, they will come to collect, and you will be in the middle). <br /> <br /> 2) twist the mind of your moral vampire. Is all well and good go and try to be super nice... but he is a Nosferatu. Let the Nightmare come to him, and twist him in return. <br /> <br /> And after all that, let us know how is going!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:57:45-07:00","id":952199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952098#post952098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quote you posted kind of... proves your point wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know how you think it proves me wrong when it says the rules for disciplines then adds in in the very next line ADDITIONAL RULES for the clan specific disciplines. Sometimes there is more than one rule for things. Like so many times when it says. This is how it works, Except when this is happening. Then these rules apply too.<br /> <br /> The books or even just the clan chapters explaining each clan and their uniqueness explains why they are protected and harder to get.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952166#post952166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of indicated in the text, though not stated directly that I know of, that each strain of vampires started out very different from the others. Over time, with the intermingling of blood, they became as similar as they are now. The prime example of this from wherever I first heard this theory is the bonus clan presented in the Tokyo setting in 2e.<br /> <br /> Every Discipline except the Clan ones are common enough that any given vampire's blood might manifest the ability naturally (or, if you like teaching, by trying to force the matter with a teacher).<br /> <br /> Of those, certain Clans manifest certain Disciplines more often than others, perhaps as a reflection of their origins. These are in-clan Disciplines. They're just more common.<br /> <br /> Of these, each Clan has a unique Discipline that originated from their bloodline (in the general sense, not the specific Bloodline sense) which only that Clan manifests naturally. For a vampire of another Clan to manifest this ability, they need some of blood that has already manifested that ability to intermingle with their own. This is because it isn't an ability found in the blood and beast of other clans.<br /> <br /> A Bloodline is what happens when a vampire has blood potent enough that it can start passing on its traits almost like Clan blood can, whatever those traits were be. Based, as one might imagine, upon its founder.<br /> <br /> It's basically magic genetics. Magic because Vampire genetics are passed down by blood, not actual genes, and you can integrate the blood of other vampires into your own magic-blood-genes by ingesting it. Some things (Clan disciplines that are not your own) do not pass down to your Childer unless you create a new bloodline to make your own magic-blood-genes more potent.<br /> <br /> Granted, there's a lot of leaps of logic from the book in that, but it's my interpretation, and it's a good enough way to explain it for those who wanted an explanation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though if you're feeding Vitae to your new Childer to Embrace them, wouldn't they have access to any Out-of-Clan Disciplines in your blood? Maybe! I don't think that's clarified anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And to your edit, yes. Graitus? said that too. sometimes knowing an out of clan discipline is as easy as &quot;My sire knew it&quot; But in this character's creation. he has no sire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-16-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:56:37-07:00","id":952300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952199#post952199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont know how you think it proves me wrong when it says the rules for disciplines then adds in in the very next line ADDITIONAL RULES for the clan specific disciplines. Sometimes there is more than one rule for things. Like so many times when it says. This is how it works, Except when this is happening. Then these rules apply too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bolded the relevant part, Vitalis. Here, again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. </b></i> </div> </div> </div>Kindred spontaneously manifest their Disciplines, indicating they are innate and you can just 'poof' and learn them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:28:03-07:00","id":952422,"title":"","content":"They spontaneously manifest disciplines that are of their clan. Nowhere does it say they innately manifest the clan unique disciplines of another clan. Technically it doesn't even say you can manifest the other common out-of-clan disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:46:01-07:00","id":952476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952183#post952183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion? I'd allow it and go for it. Yeah, the bit about having Protean 2 from start is not following RAW, but well, why not? The aspect you've picked is pretty horrifying, certainly, and the Blood twists the Nosferatu in weird ways. I feel the horror potential coming from this child.<br /> <br /> My two cents would be:<br /> <br /> 1) allow the ST to infect your character with a Gangrel Blood Bond (maybe it could have been a fight in the slaughter house the night you arrived, and now the character is claiming that territory. AS a Gangrel, he could well regard you as a threat ... or as a pupil. Besides, his/her Blood would some vampires in you already. If she/he has enemies, they will come to collect, and you will be in the middle). <br /> <br /> 2) twist the mind of your moral vampire. Is all well and good go and try to be super nice... but he is a Nosferatu. Let the Nightmare come to him, and twist him in return. <br /> <br /> And after all that, let us know how is going!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, his point is that he is a fairly innocent kid that will be forced to adapt to life as a monster. He will become cold, but occasionally have flashes of compassion. My ultimate goal is for him to become a tragic monster that does horrifying things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:26:12-07:00","id":952501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952422#post952422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They spontaneously manifest disciplines that are of their clan. Nowhere does it say they innately manifest the clan unique disciplines of another clan. Technically it doesn't even say you can manifest the other common out-of-clan disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half of the rules are being ignored at this point. I do not think it matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Water is a liquid. When Water reaches a temperature below the freezing point, water becomes a solid. Some people are choosing to only read the first sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:51:02-07:00","id":952612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=952476#post952476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, his point is that he is a fairly innocent kid that will be forced to adapt to life as a monster. He will become cold, but occasionally have flashes of compassion. My ultimate goal is for him to become a tragic monster that does horrifying things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve of this. Feel to me like you've grasped the VtR spirit fairly good. Go forth and have fun! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:12:35-07:00","id":953054,"title":"","content":"That moment when a Vampire game is going heavy homebrew to ignore core rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:49:40-07:00","id":953206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953054#post953054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That moment when a Vampire game is going heavy homebrew to ignore core rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am just following character creation rules. The storyteller house ruled how our characters were embraced (though there is precedent for it in the book) And I am paying the out of clan price for my discipline. As for my protean stuff, it says to work with the storyteller over the details of making new predatory aspects. I doubt our game is any more customised than anyone elses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:31:47-07:00","id":953274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953206#post953206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am just following character creation rules. The storyteller house ruled how our characters were embraced (though there is precedent for it in the book) And I am paying the out of clan price for my discipline. As for my protean stuff, it says to work with the storyteller over the details of making new predatory aspects. I doubt our game is any more customised than anyone elses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you start with a Unique Clan discipline without having any of the blood bonding, vitae addiction, drinking vampire blood consequences, it's going against RAW. I hate to point that out.. again. But I feel like that whole second sentence with additional rules for the unique disciplines is being completely utterly ignored. There are rules for disciplines, then ADDITIONAL rules for UNIQUE disciplines. I would like to point out that Rose Bailey did not tell any of us we were wrong in &quot;My clan for your clan&quot; Thread. She even mentioned bloodbonding being a perversion... <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=935125#post935125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing wrong with players doing it... but keep in mind that vampires mutually swapping blood is called &quot;perversion&quot; by Kindred culture in general, and looked down on. Probably because of the behavior that kind of weird love tends to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...o-expect/page2</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I will mention again though, If you know it's not RAW and your storyteller is homebrewing the OK and whatever else you want to homebrew, that is totally cool. Just be aware if you walk into another group and they say not allowed, then you are aware of why. Honestly story tellers can do whatever they want as long as everyone is having fun...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-18-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:52:18-07:00","id":953288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for my protean stuff, it says to work with the storyteller over the details of making new predatory aspects. I doubt our game is any more customised than anyone else's. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, feeding lamprey tentacles with the ability to not only feed but also Venom/Carnage web-swing would fall heavily in the category of Vicissitude 6+ in the World of Darkness. Protean is bringing a part of the beast out of you and manifesting it, so you grow wings, claws, senses, shift your form. Turning your entire self INTO a lamprey seems vaguely viable, but Protean is about your changing form coming out, not about spawning another creature out of yourself. Tentacles work, as said before, but even then, if you want greater function for them, you're really looking at Protean 4, and then there's considering whether or not you have the strength to even vault yourself like that. Consider how many people can't even manage a single rep of a solid form pull-up. <br /> <br /> Then there's Humanity... considering learning a dot of Cruac is a low level trigger, I would say something this nightmarish definitely falls in the guidelines of needing to roll for degeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:05:04-07:00","id":953372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953274#post953274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When you start with a Unique Clan discipline without having any of the blood bonding, vitae addiction, drinking vampire blood consequences, it's going against RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't against RAW. The rules do not state that you start blood bound if you start with an out-of-clan Discipline.<br /> <br /> Remember that starting characters weren't Embraced yesterday. It only takes a year for a blood bond to fade. It's very possible that the bond faded before the game begins. Or that one of the various methods to remove or prevent a Bond was used on the character.<br /> <br /> That said, this particular character seems a lot newer than that. It does seem a bit questionable how they both found someone to teach it and let the Blood Bond fade so early in their Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:27:47-07:00","id":953388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953372#post953372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really isn't against RAW. The rules do not state that you start blood bound if you start with an out-of-clan Discipline.<br /> <br /> Remember that starting characters weren't Embraced yesterday. It only takes a year for a blood bond to fade. It's very possible that the bond faded before the game begins. Or that one of the various methods to remove or prevent a Bond was used on the character.<br /> <br /> That said, this particular character seems a lot newer than that. It does seem a bit questionable how they both found someone to teach it and let the Blood Bond fade so early in their Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did not say you start with one, I am saying you start with all the potential consequences of DRINKING ANOTHER VAMPIRE'S BLOOD which include bonding and addiction.<br /> <br /> You arent taking into account what this character is when created. You are only reading part of the information here. I have said that starting with a unique clan discipline sometimes is as easy as &quot;my sire could do it&quot; then problem solved. I have said this. Or even That it's been years, the blood has been drank and the bond has faded because that's what you wrote in the back story. RAW ( even you stated so in the other thread which i linked ) You have to drink the vampire's blood to get unique clan disciplines.<br /> <br /> This particular character was spontaneously embraced as a Nosferatu with 2 dots of Protean ( maybe changed to 1 dot now ). and Literally was born yesterday...<br /> <br /> Please read everything before you tell me I am wrong again. I wasnt Saying its RAW to start with a blood bond, I was saying it's RAW to have to drink another vampire's blood to learn a unique clan discipline and to not do that is against RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-18-2016, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:29:50-07:00","id":953449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953274#post953274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When you start with a Unique Clan discipline without having any of the blood bonding, vitae addiction, drinking vampire blood consequences, it's going against RAW. I hate to point that out.. again. But I feel like that whole second sentence with additional rules for the unique disciplines is being completely utterly ignored. There are rules for disciplines, then ADDITIONAL rules for UNIQUE disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, first of all none of these bloodborne, vitae adicction consequeces are mentioned during the character creation chapter, which led both me and my storyteller to read them way later in the book and conclude that if these consequeces applied to character creation, they would be there. We thought this was in game stuff, not related to character creation decisions, but this is our first time so maybe we are wrong.<br /> <br /> Secondly, what are you talking about when you mention unique disciplines? I'm just using Protean, with different predatory aspects on. the second dot, the book even says to make up new ones with the storyteller. I'm starting to think that VtR could use a third edition to put relevant information in the right chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:46:43-07:00","id":953457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953449#post953449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, first of all none of these bloodborne, vitae adicction consequeces are mentioned during the character creation chapter, which led both me and my storyteller to read them way later in the book and conclude that if these consequeces applied to character creation, they would be there. We thought this was in game stuff, not related to character creation decisions, but this is our first time so maybe we are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Character creation is assumed to be making a vampire that has existed long enough for those consequences to not be in play at that point. They are not the rules for making a freshly Embraced Kindred. If you make a freshly Embraced then stuff that would otherwise be in-game becomes character creation considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953449#post953449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, what are you talking about when you mention unique disciplines? I'm just using Protean, with different predatory aspects on. the second dot, the book even says to make up new ones with the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>They mean Clan Unique disciplines; Disciplines carried by only one clan such as Protean. Any one knowing it outside the Gangrel is special and requires them having drunk the blood of someone who already had it. That is above and beyond all other rules for gaining Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953449#post953449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to think that VtR could use a third edition to put relevant information in the right chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The CofD books are written the way they are for specific reasons, they aren't in the 'wrong' chapter, just not the one you would expect maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixed Quote block 08-18-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:42:04-07:00","id":953562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953449#post953449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, first of all none of these bloodborne, vitae adicction consequeces are mentioned during the character creation chapter, which led both me and my storyteller to read them way later in the book and conclude that if these consequeces applied to character creation, they would be there. We thought this was in game stuff, not related to character creation decisions, but this is our first time so maybe we are wrong.<br /> <br /> Secondly, what are you talking about when you mention unique disciplines? I'm just using Protean, with different predatory aspects on. the second dot, the book even says to make up new ones with the storyteller. I'm starting to think that VtR could use a third edition to put relevant information in the right chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have been told in this thread several times that Protean is Gangrel clan specific. ( and not just by me )<br /> Dominate Is Ventrue<br /> Majesty is Daeva<br /> Nightmare is Nosferatu<br /> Auspex is Mehket.<br /> <br /> ^ those are Unique clan specific disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would like to point out in any roll playing game that you play even 5th edition dnd you can not build a character off of 1 single page. You have to look in multiple areas through out the book. It's not that it is organized poorly. I think that perhaps you started to play without reading the book. Which is fine ( i have done this for 5th dnd )<br /> <br /> The character creation chapter assumes that you have read the rest of the book and thus will apply your knowledge accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:23:38-07:00","id":953579,"title":"","content":"If you're really set on him having Protean out of the gate, then I'd have to agree that you just remake him as a Gangrel. You wouldn't even have to change his personality all that much, since both Gangrel and Nosferatu have a tendency to avoid society. Nossies because they have little choice in the matter, and Gangrel because they're survival experts.<br /> <br /> Vigor may be an out of clan discipline, but it's not a clan unique discipline, so your character would be able to learn it without drinking anybody's blood. Which would make it much easier to explain without having to rewrite your backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other words, you can pull off the same character concept easier as a Gangrel, than you can as a Nosferatu. Since the latter option requires a bunch of home brewing and a more in depth backstory than what you currently have available.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>P.S:</b> Unique disciplines are written on the clans in <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>italics</i></span> like so. They are also the signature ability of their respective clans, and they don't just go handing them out to anybody who wants to learn them. At least not without exacting some sort of price for that knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-23-2016, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:47:43-07:00","id":953594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953562#post953562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have been told in this thread several times that Protean is Gangrel clan specific. ( and not just by me )<br /> Dominate Is Ventrue<br /> Majesty is Daeva<br /> Nightmare is Nosferatu<br /> Auspex is Mehket.<br /> <br /> ^ those are Unique clan specific disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would like to point out in any roll playing game that you play even 5th edition dnd you can not build a character off of 1 single page. You have to look in multiple areas through out the book. It's not that it is organized poorly. I think that perhaps you started to play without reading the book. Which is fine ( i have done this for 5th dnd )<br /> <br /> The character creation chapter assumes that you have read the rest of the book and thus will apply your knowledge accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most players don't read the whole book, and while I agree that you need to go to parts of the book that outline certain abilities, it would have been nice it there was a disclaimer that the out of clan disciplines require a hell of a lot of red tape that need to be read in depth. At least if I was writing it I would give a quick cautionary sentence and site the page numbers that go into more detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:50:44-07:00","id":953597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953579#post953579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're really set on him having Protean out of the gate, then I'd have to agree that you just remake him as a Gangrel. You wouldn't even have to change his personality all that much, since both Gangrel and Nosferatu have a tendency to be avoid society. Nossies because they have little choice in the matter, and Gangrel because they're survival experts.<br /> <br /> Vigor may be an out of clan discipline, but it's not a clan unique discipline, so your character would be able to learn it without drinking anybody's blood. Which would make it much easier to explain without having to rewrite your backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other words, you can pull off the same character concept easier as a Gangrel, than you can as a Nosferatu. Since the latter option requires a bunch of home brewing and a more in depth backstory than what you currently have available.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>P.S:</b> Unique disciplines are written on the clans in <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>italics</i></span> like so. They are also the signature ability of their respective clans, and they don't just go handing them out to anybody who wants to learn them. At least not without exacting some sort of price for that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really can't, because this character is supposed to have trouble hiding his vampire nature with his black eyes, an all. Also I like the clan bane, it just sounds fun to have dramatic failures happen by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:53:39-07:00","id":953600,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty dead set on playing a Nosferatu. And I really don't want Protean anyway (rather have nightmare), but I still like the tenticle idea, so I homebrewed a merit that adds to the physical deformities that Nosferatu can manifest. My Storyteller likes the merit, although he said he might make some changes.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Graveworm</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOO, or OOOOO</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Must be Nosferatu.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For some Haunts, the curse manifest as a physical thing by warping their body in such a way that is visibly grotesque, but for others it's much worse. Your Beast is not content to simply writhe within your soul, it emerges in physical form. You have one or more orifices on your body, that nest a round, sucking, maw. By spending a Vitae, the maw emerges, revealing a long, leech-like parasite, often in a gout of blood. The worm (or worms) can be used as another pair arms or legs, giving you a better reach for climbing, and the ability to grapple at a distance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrible Reach</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOO</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) The worm (or worms) are 10 meters long, and extends your reach to accomplish any task that doesn't require much manual dexterity. For example: Slipping it through prison bars to grab a prison guards keys would be appropriate, while operating a keyboard or firing a gun would not. This appendage is strong enough to bear your weight, and can be used to help you climb 10 meters as a reflexive action (Storyteller wants this to be a move action at half your speed instead, seems reasonable). The worm can also be used to used for an unarmed attack, or grapple up to 10 meters away. When grappling your victim may only attempt to use the Break Free, or Damage moves while grappled. If you take damage in any of your last three hit boxes (Bashing, Lethal, or Agitated) the grapple ends, and you get the Arm Wrack Tilt, giving you a -2 penalty to using these appendages for all physical actions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hungry Maw</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOOOO</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) The worm is not just a sucking mouth, but has grown a ring of hooked fangs. This Maw is always hungry, and is visible on your body unless covered by clothing. If touched it may attempt to bite, and cause a dramatic failure on affected social rolls related to physical intimacy. This maw can be used to feed during a grapple up to 10 meters away.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:23:17-07:00","id":953619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953597#post953597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really can't, because this character is supposed to have trouble hiding his vampire nature with his black eyes, an all. Also I like the clan bane, it just sounds fun to have dramatic failures happen by accident.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And you couldn't give a Gangrel some sort of raccoon mask? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, there are several animals who have black eyes. Lobsters come to mind, for starters.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you said you're set on playing a Nosferatu. Can't blame you, really, as they're my favorite clan in Requiem, followed by Gangrel in second place.<br /> <br /> But like you, I've skimmed through the book rather than reading the whole thing. And it seems like the more experienced players are in agreement that this would be difficult / impossible to pull off without reworking the core mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>P.S:</b> The Nosferatu don't have to be physically deformed in Requiem (like they did in Masquerade). They can still retain their human form, but be disturbing in other fashions. They could smell like a rotting corpse, act socially deplorable, or generate some kind of palpable aura that unnerves people in their vicinity. The only consistency with their bane is that people don't like being around them. But that doesn't mean they have to be ugly to achieve that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-18-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:59:40-07:00","id":953643,"title":"","content":"<b>P.S:</b> The Nosferatu don't have to be physically deformed in Requiem (like they did in Masquerade). They can still retain their human form, but be disturbing in other fashions. They could smell like a rotting corpse, act socially deplorable, or generate some kind of palpable aura that unnerves people in their vicinity. The only consistency with their bane is that people don't like being around them. But that doesn't mean they have to be ugly to achieve that effect.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I know they don't have to be physically deformed or ugly, in fact on first inspection you would only notice a good looking if pale kid, until you see his eyes. Ever heard the black eye kids legend? Its probably the closest the west has come to one of those weird Japanese urban legends. Seemed like Nosferatu represents it best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T21:12:24-07:00","id":953648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953643#post953643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know they don't have to be physically deformed or ugly, in fact on first inspection you would only notice a good looking if pale kid, until you see his eyes. Ever heard the black eye kids legend? Its probably the closest the west has come to one of those weird Japanese urban legends. Seemed like Nosferatu represents it best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I haven't. At least not in any detail great enough to memorize it. I do know of a black toothed woman legend that comes from Japan, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:14:46-07:00","id":953736,"title":"","content":"Make the character part of a bloodline that favors protean. Done.<br /> <br /> Or go with the merits, if the ST likes it. I feel like you could just take &quot;I have maws&quot; as a one or two dot merit, then back up its climbing and moving prowess with the parkour merit.<br /> <br /> Make it two dots, its effect being the +10 meter reach. Then take Parkour.<br /> <br /> Oh. Totally keep the &quot;bites people on a dramatic failure&quot; drawback. Its amusing and fluffy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-19-2016, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:48:35-07:00","id":953764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953736#post953736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make the character part of a bloodline that favors protean. Done.<br /> <br /> Or go with the merits, if the ST likes it. I feel like you could just take &amp;quot;I have maws&amp;quot; as a one or two dot merit, then back up its climbing and moving prowess with the parkour merit.<br /> <br /> Make it two dots, its effect being the +10 meter reach. Then take Parkour.<br /> <br /> Oh. Totally keep the &amp;quot;bites people on a dramatic failure&amp;quot; drawback. Its amusing and fluffy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two dots for the ten meter reach, with the grappling stuff? That... seems really powerful for two dots doesn't it? I mean, these tenticals are basically lifting the victim off the ground so they can only use break free and damage. Also vampires can do lethal damage while grappled by using their fangs to attack, the maw allows you to do that at a distance for the five dot version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:51:58-07:00","id":953766,"title":"","content":"Make it two dots with the effect being the 10 meter reach. Dont change the grapple rules for the opponent. Note the tentacles can bite + feed like the vampire's mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:03:30-07:00","id":953811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953766#post953766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it two dots with the effect being the 10 meter reach. Dont change the grapple rules for the opponent. Note the tentacles can bite + feed like the vampire's mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how they could do those other grapple moves from 10 meters away. Just try to visualize it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:35:07-07:00","id":953830,"title":"","content":"Break free: normal<br /> Damage: atyack the tentacles<br /> Drop Prone: drag you to the ground by tebtacles<br /> Hold: Pull you off balance by tebtaclrs<br /> Restrain: tie you up with your own tentacles<br /> Cover: pull you in front of a gun by your tebtacles.<br /> <br /> That said, having them pulled in when grappled would be easier on the suspension of disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:45:40-07:00","id":953837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953594#post953594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most players don't read the whole book, and while I agree that you need to go to parts of the book that outline certain abilities, it would have been nice it there was a disclaimer that the out of clan disciplines require a hell of a lot of red tape that need to be read in depth. At least if I was writing it I would give a quick cautionary sentence and site the page numbers that go into more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 15 Daeva: &quot;Disciplines: Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Vigor&quot;<br /> Page 19 Gangrel: Disciplines: Animalism, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> Page 22 Mehket: &quot;Disciplines: <i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> Page 25 Nosferatu: &quot;Disciplines: <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Vigor.&quot; <br /> <br /> You might ask yourself why these are in italics. If you dont read the whole book, I hope at least you read the Nosferatu section. They probably assumed you would go looking in the discipline section for what that meant. Which is page 125<br /> <br /> <br /> Page 28 Ventrue: &quot;Disciplines: Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <br /> Page 81 Disciplines: Right before the quick guide on page 82 <br /> <br /> <i>Choose three dots in Disciplines. At least two must be<br /> from the vampire\u2019s in-clan Disciplines. The third dot may<br /> be from any Discipline. <b>If you choose a third Discipline dot from a non-clan Discipline, consider how your character<br /> learned it. Did she have a mentor? Did she steal the blood of another clan?</b></i><br /> <br /> Page 125 Disciplines<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953736#post953736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make the character part of a bloodline that favors protean. Done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering he had no sire ( cant join at BP 1 ) and has no blood ties ( cant join at 2 ) He would have to wait until BP 4 to join a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Page 98<br /> <br /> &quot;At Blood Potency 4, any<br /> vampire of her clan may act as an Avus. An Avus is a sort of<br /> mentor. Acting as an Avus into a bloodline requires feeding the<br /> prospect at least one point of Vitae.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:31:59-07:00","id":953859,"title":"","content":"The spontanious embrace is being ST mandated. Spontaniously being wmbraced as a bloodline is just as much in the rules as the spontanious embrace as a non-revenant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:36:44-07:00","id":953863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953859#post953859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spontanious embrace is being ST mandated. Spontaniously being wmbraced as a bloodline is just as much in the rules as the spontanious embrace as a non-revenant</div> </div> </div> </div>Page98<br /> <i>&quot;Kindred may join bloodlines as allowed by their Blood<br /> Potency dots. A character may join her sire\u2019s bloodline at Blood<br /> Potency 1. At Blood Potency 2, a vampire with which she shares<br /> a blood tie (see p. 98) may act as Avus.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> How can you do that ^ , if you have no sire? He cant have brothers and sisters without a sire? I am not saying you cant be spontaneously embraced. What I said was, if he wants to be in a bloodline he will have to wait to BP 4 to find a Nos to induct him into that Bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:34:40-07:00","id":953887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953837#post953837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 15 Daeva: &quot;Disciplines: Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Vigor&quot;<br /> Page 19 Gangrel: Disciplines: Animalism, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> Page 22 Mehket: &quot;Disciplines: <i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> Page 25 Nosferatu: &quot;Disciplines: <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate, Vigor.&quot;<br /> <br /> You might ask yourself why these are in italics. If you dont read the whole book, I hope at least you read the Nosferatu section. They probably assumed you would go looking in the discipline section for what that meant. Which is page 125<br /> <br /> <br /> Page 28 Ventrue: &quot;Disciplines: Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <br /> Page 81 Disciplines: Right before the quick guide on page 82<br /> <br /> <i>Choose three dots in Disciplines. At least two must be<br /> from the vampire\u2019s in-clan Disciplines. The third dot may<br /> be from any Discipline. <b>If you choose a third Discipline dot from a non-clan Discipline, consider how your character<br /> learned it. Did she have a mentor? Did she steal the blood of another clan?</b></i><br /> <br /> Page 125 Disciplines<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Considering he had no sire ( cant join at BP 1 ) and has no blood ties ( cant join at 2 ) He would have to wait until BP 4 to join a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Page 98<br /> <br /> &quot;At Blood Potency 4, any<br /> vampire of her clan may act as an Avus. An Avus is a sort of<br /> mentor. Acting as an Avus into a bloodline requires feeding the<br /> prospect at least one point of Vitae.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken, what do you think of the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:09:03-07:00","id":953945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953887#post953887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Graveworm</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOO, or OOOOO</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Must be Nosferatu.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: For some Haunts, the curse manifest as a physical thing by warping their body in such a way that is visibly grotesque, but for others it's much worse.<br /> Your Beast is not content to simply writhe within your soul, it emerges in physical form. You have one or more orifices on your body, that nest a round, sucking, maw. By spending a Vitae, the maw emerges, revealing a long, leech-like parasite, often in a gout of blood. The worm (or worms) can be used as another pair arms or legs, giving you a better reach for climbing, and the ability to grapple at a distance.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know if this has been said or not, but this is Protean. Transforming and twisting your body to give you animal like abilities. So for 3-5 experience you are doing what Protean 2 could do - that's 6-8 experience. Based on just that I dont think this = Merit = is fair.<br /> <br /> I try to shy away from making merits to do things Disciplines can already do and I never make merits that alter disciplines. If you want to Alter a discipline to do more or make it better. You make a devotion(page 142) I would probably make this Protean 2 and Vigor 1 1 dot devotion 1 experience. ( for the 3 dot version of this merit )<br /> For the 5 dot version of this merit I would say 4 protean and 1 vigor devotion ( for 2 exp )<br /> <br /> Edit: there is one merit that alters protean Claws of the unholy. prereq. Protean 4<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953887#post953887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrible Reach (</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOO</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) The worm (or worms) are 10 meters long, and extends your reach to accomplish any task that doesn't require much manual dexterity. For example: Slipping it through prison bars to grab a prison guards keys would be appropriate, while operating a keyboard or firing a gun would not. This appendage is strong enough to bear your weight, and can be used to help you climb 10 meters as a reflexive action (Storyteller wants this to be a move action at half your speed instead, seems reasonable). The worm can also be used to used for an unarmed attack, or grapple up to 10 meters away. When grappling your victim may only attempt to use the Break Free, or Damage moves while grappled. If you take damage in any of your last three hit boxes (Bashing, Lethal, or Agitated) the grapple ends, and you get the Arm Wrack Tilt, giving you a -2 penalty to using these appendages for all physical actions.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As for what it does Mechanically. 10 meters is about 30 feet. Which is about a 2 story building.. So you could grab someone off a roof and pull them down? That to me seems a little over powered. 10 feet is more acceptable.<br /> <br /> Climbing 10 meters as a reflexive action. is Celerity. you would have to be moving so fast... I agree with storyteller, make it a Move action as you are moving. seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Using the appendage as a fist instead seems fine, but again I am not ok with grappling someone so very far away. Though the additional grapple mechanics seem acceptable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953887#post953887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hungry Maw (OOOOO</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) The worm is not just a sucking mouth, but has grown a ring of hooked fangs. This Maw is always hungry, and is visible on your body unless covered by clothing. If touched it may attempt to bite, and cause a dramatic failure on affected social rolls related to physical intimacy. This maw can be used to feed during a grapple up to 10 meters away.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Again I am not ok with feeding off someone who is on the ground while you are on the roof. It is too far. I would say 10 FEET at most, but to be able to feed at a distance like the Strain vampires. Seems worth a devotion and kind of cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is my opinion.<br /> <br /> Second Edit: I made something to feed from a distance for my game, but it was a 5th dot Discipline so it took 15 exp to get...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:45:30-07:00","id":953965,"title":"","content":"5 Meters might be more reasonable. My whole idea for this merit was it to be more of a Nosferatu thing because they are often described as being physically different. I think in the clan introduction it even mention one with six arms that climbed on the ceiling like a spider. I thought it was a shame that there aren't any Nosferatu disciplines that take advantage of their altered bodies. This is why the maws never go away like they would in protean. <br /> <br /> Besides that I just thought the image of hunters runing through a wearhouse or down the street and these worms busting through windows to latch onto their heads, or pull them away from their allies seems really cool, especially since any vampire could hear their heartbeats, and smell their blood to locate them out of site. I would be like hand fishing for hunters \ud83d\ude09. <br /> <br /> On a side note there are several merits that change how disciplines work, the one that come to mind is swarm form. Do you just find altering disciplines with merits distastful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:50:43-07:00","id":953966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953863#post953863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page98<br /> <i>&amp;quot;Kindred may join bloodlines as allowed by their Blood<br /> Potency dots. A character may join her sire\u2019s bloodline at Blood<br /> Potency 1. At Blood Potency 2, a vampire with which she shares<br /> a blood tie (see p. 98) may act as Avus.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> How can you do that ^ , if you have no sire? He cant have brothers and sisters without a sire? I am not saying you cant be spontaneously embraced. What I said was, if he wants to be in a bloodline he will have to wait to BP 4 to find a Nos to induct him into that Bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same way you spontaniously embrace straight into a clan. ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:59:26-07:00","id":953974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953965#post953965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 Meters might be more reasonable. My whole idea for this merit was it to be more of a Nosferatu thing because they are often described as being physically different. I think in the clan introduction it even mention one with six arms that climbed on the ceiling like a spider. I thought it was a shame that there aren't any Nosferatu disciplines that take advantage of their altered bodies. This is why the maws never go away like they would in protean.<br /> <br /> Besides that I just thought the image of hunters runing through a wearhouse or down the street and these worms busting through windows to latch onto their heads, or pull them away from their allies seems really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and Gangrel are more animalistic. Not all Nosferatu are physically different in 2E. I wouldnt even say &quot;most&quot; are. which is why I think there isnt anything that plays on that. Nosferatu at their core are terrifying. They prey upon that fear. They live on that fear. That's why their clan discipline is Nightmare. They make you THINK there are giant 6 armed people crawling on the ceiling like spiders..<br /> <br /> Protean 3 you could stay an animal indefinitely<br /> <br /> I agree with you that this is doable and it seems a lot of fun. I just think you and I have 2 different ways of going about it. If your story teller gives you the go. have fun with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953966#post953966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same way you spontaniously embrace straight into a clan. ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again you are allowed to homebrew anything you want. Dump as many rules as you want. Do whatever you want, but RAW can't be done. <br /> <br /> As long as you know it's not RAW and are swinging with it anyway. Fine. but dont claim it to be within the rules when it's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-19-2016, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:47:49-07:00","id":954099,"title":"","content":"Vitalis is being pretty generous in suggesting 'only' protean 2 and vigor 1.<br /> <br /> Frankly with what you're describing in that merit, I would push for Protean 4, and Vigor 3 as a START. To me, you're not describing something that is starting-level. You're describing something wholly unique and terrible that would bring out horrors and legends across kindred society and beyond.<br /> <br /> That is simply beyond starting vampire power-base. Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners covers characters and powers like what you're describing and these are the things that Sires tell their Childer about to keep them in line for centuries.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I don't like your idea. I'm saying it's something to aspire to, not start with.<br /> <br /> As you develop this further, I would say the higher level functions DO require Nightmare (probably 2 plus), yes, two SEPARATE clan-Unique disciplines and the story by which you develop something like that should not be skimmed over, glossed quickly and should take decades if not centuries to develop.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't make me okay with it by any scope as again, this is breaching.<br /> <br /> If you want to see the scope of which I'm talking just take a look at Holger, and really let everything about him from his background to his actual powers sink in a little bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Frankly, the more I think about it, a devotion/merit like this also probably should require at LEAST Blood Potency 3 to learn/develop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","user":"CrimsonOwl","date":". 08-19-2016, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:28:31-07:00","id":954118,"title":"","content":"Jumping off of CrimsonOwl's point about scope, and acknowledging the talk of bloodlines and blood potency, might I suggest considering raising the power-level the game starts at.<br /> <br /> The advantage is that you could more easily create a horror with terrifying capabilities as your 'budget' wouldn't be nearly as constrained, plus you could take a bloodline if you up your Blood Potency. Fellow players could then build characters strong enough to compensate, the ST can build around your power, you get to play the character you want, and In-World, there is no reason you couldn't have spontaneously embraced with that power. The others and ST merely have to acknowledge the freakishness of it all.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T19:20:26-07:00","id":954149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=954118#post954118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jumping off of CrimsonOwl's point about scope, and acknowledging the talk of bloodlines and blood potency, might I suggest considering raising the power-level the game starts at.<br /> <br /> The advantage is that you could more easily create a horror with terrifying capabilities as your 'budget' wouldn't be nearly as constrained, plus you could take a bloodline if you up your Blood Potency. Fellow players could then build characters strong enough to compensate, the ST can build around your power, you get to play the character you want, and In-World, there is no reason you couldn't have spontaneously embraced with that power. The others and ST merely have to acknowledge the freakishness of it all.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could actually get behind that notion. Make the dots reflect what you want to play, and bring everyone else along as well, let them be whatever they're wanting to be, otherwise, I know I'd be feeling awfully left out if I were one of the other players.<br /> <br /> For additional reference material, I present Vicissitude from Dark Ages: Vampire (Which is NOT Chronicles of Darkness):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dark Ages: Vampire (Player's Guide to the High Clans) Vicissitude &quot;6&quot;. Graft Life to Life: With normal Vicissitude, a Tzimisce may take the arm from one person and graft it to another, but the recipient is unable to control the arm and it soon begins to decay. With this power, the user may take body parts from living creatures and graft them onto others, living or undead, and allow for the recipient to use the new limb. Exceptionally monstrous and distrubing creatures can be created with this power or one may graft extra organs into others, allowing them to function longer while wounded.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:16:02-07:00","id":954218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrimsonOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=954099#post954099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitalis is being pretty generous in suggesting 'only' protean 2 and vigor 1.<br /> <br /> Frankly with what you're describing in that merit, I would push for Protean 4, and Vigor 3 as a START. To me, you're not describing something that is starting-level. You're describing something wholly unique and terrible that would bring out horrors and legends across kindred society and beyond.<br /> <br /> That is simply beyond starting vampire power-base. Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners covers characters and powers like what you're describing and these are the things that Sires tell their Childer about to keep them in line for centuries.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I don't like your idea. I'm saying it's something to aspire to, not start with.<br /> <br /> As you develop this further, I would say the higher level functions DO require Nightmare (probably 2 plus), yes, two SEPARATE clan-Unique disciplines and the story by which you develop something like that should not be skimmed over, glossed quickly and should take decades if not centuries to develop.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't make me okay with it by any scope as again, this is breaching.<br /> <br /> If you want to see the scope of which I'm talking just take a look at Holger, and really let everything about him from his background to his actual powers sink in a little bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Frankly, the more I think about it, a devotion/merit like this also probably should require at LEAST Blood Potency 3 to learn/develop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's Holger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:04:03-07:00","id":954422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=954218#post954218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's Holger?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's a character in Night Horrors: Immortal sinners, alongside the Unholy, the kindred the Merit &quot;Claws of the Unholy&quot; is named after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T01:48:17-07:00","id":956210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=953594#post953594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most players don't read the whole book, and while I agree that you need to go to parts of the book that outline certain abilities, it would have been nice it there was a disclaimer that the out of clan disciplines require a hell of a lot of red tape that need to be read in depth. At least if I was writing it I would give a quick cautionary sentence and site the page numbers that go into more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If most players don't read the book then why does every single person in this thread giving you answers seem to all have read the book. Not reading the book is litterally just playing a game with no knowledge and no investment into the lore. It guts the experience.<br /> <br /> As well as your merit is so just protean but heavily modified its unfunny, espicially graplling from ten meters away. Come on man the reason Gangrel have protean is that there the only ones that can change there form and give usually very static undead flesh motion. Giving your character an innate ability to grapple from ten meters away not only would be a massive breach of the masqurade, but makes it so nothing can stop outrun you. Vampire is a game of horror, of knowing you've lost your humanity and clinging to those last vestiges of being human, only your character seems to not care what so ever and wishes to be as monstorous as possible which, in most polite Kindred cities would have you watched for possible breaches.<br /> <br /> A regular Nosferatu is a great clan, they make excellent fighters, and great stealth, and there really is no need to add that much to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:28:14-07:00","id":956257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956210#post956210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If most players don't read the book then why does every single person in this thread giving you answers seem to all have read the book. Not reading the book is litterally just playing a game with no knowledge and no investment into the lore. It guts the experience.<br /> <br /> As well as your merit is so just protean but heavily modified its unfunny, espicially graplling from ten meters away. Come on man the reason Gangrel have protean is that there the only ones that can change there form and give usually very static undead flesh motion. Giving your character an innate ability to grapple from ten meters away not only would be a massive breach of the masqurade, but makes it so nothing can stop outrun you. Vampire is a game of horror, of knowing you've lost your humanity and clinging to those last vestiges of being human, only your character seems to not care what so ever and wishes to be as monstorous as possible which, in most polite Kindred cities would have you watched for possible breaches.<br /> <br /> A regular Nosferatu is a great clan, they make excellent fighters, and great stealth, and there really is no need to add that much to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for being creative. I was almost enjoying myself for a moment there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:35:22-07:00","id":956290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956257#post956257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for being creative. I was almost enjoying myself for a moment there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take it too hard. You clearly have an understanding of mechanics and how to put a theme together. I personally wouldn't let the merit fly at my table, but I prefer political games with flashpoints of action. For a high adventure style game it could fit, and as has been pointed out - the only worthwhile 'value' judgment will be the type of game your table is playing. Ultimately it doesn't matter what I think unless you come play with me.<br /> <br /> Still, I do think you could work on balance considerations. If what you are creating essentially makes an end-run around existing powers (Protean in this case) you really should think long and hard about putting it in. Add to that the fact that you are doubling down on eliminating the one big weakness of grapple (can't do it from range) AND the fact that you made it a Merit (the cheapest/easiest thing to buy) are big red flags for me and I suspect others.<br /> <br /> It fits the cool idea in your mind's eye and is internally consistent, but starts to fray when directly comparing it to other mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:04:30-07:00","id":956304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956290#post956290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't take it too hard. You clearly have an understanding of mechanics and how to put a theme together. I personally wouldn't let the merit fly at my table, but I prefer political games with flashpoints of action. For a high adventure style game it could fit, and as has been pointed out - the only worthwhile 'value' judgment will be the type of game your table is playing. Ultimately it doesn't matter what I think unless you come play with me.<br /> <br /> Still, I do think you could work on balance considerations. If what you are creating essentially makes an end-run around existing powers (Protean in this case) you really should think long and hard about putting it in. Add to that the fact that you are doubling down on eliminating the one big weakness of grapple (can't do it from range) AND the fact that you made it a Merit (the cheapest/easiest thing to buy) are big red flags for me and I suspect others.<br /> <br /> It fits the cool idea in your mind's eye and is internally consistent, but starts to fray when directly comparing it to other mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the balance issue people have with it. I don't plan on using it for that reason, what I don't understand is so many VtR fans, unwillingness to facilitate style, and (when balanced) mechanical changes to reinforce unique character ideas. If I was a Storyteller I would love my players to come up with a unique idea. The reward for that would be to modify the rules for an interesting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:12:42-07:00","id":956307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956304#post956304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the balance issue people have with it. I don't plan on using it for that reason, what I don't understand is so many VtR fans, unwillingness to facilitate style, and (when balanced) mechanical changes to reinforce unique character ideas. If I was a Storyteller I would love my players to come up with a unique idea. The reward for that would be to modify the rules for an interesting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for me and my group - a lot of our past struggles over style have been trying to break away from what we call 'Vampions' - the trap that people seem to fall into by playing Requiem more like a 'Vampires w/ Superpowers' game over a one about the struggle of personal horror and immortal politics. This merit more reminds me of a comic character - like Venom, for example - than the NPCs and PCs I usually make.<br /> <br /> I routinely work with players to come up with custom mechanics and bonuses, but I like them to fit the setting I have in place. I'm less likely to approve something that clashes with the existing or intended style. I'm more likely to do so in a new startup game, but I'd want to really talk about the style clash and hopefully work that style into the world building at the outset to eliminate the clash altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:46:26-07:00","id":956315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956257#post956257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for being creative. I was almost enjoying myself for a moment there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest, your creativity is a little bit confusing. The first part of your character description makes it seem like he hates being a vampire and tries to keep in touch with his humanity, only for the next part to reveal he's specifically trained himself to sprout tentacles that ensnare and drink people. How did he develop this ability, why does he seem okay with using it if he hates feeding on people?<br /> <br /> If your argument is that it makes it easier to feed, you should know that the Nosferatu have a reputation for being physical power houses. If something goes wrong on the stealth tactic, the Nosferatu is quite capable of making an improvised exit via smashing through a wall.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I were the ST, I would definitely say that creating tentacles with mouths on them classifies as a Humanity breach. Any vampire who's willing to learn that ability would not be able to function at the level you're planning to use. In fact, it sounds like something that Belial's Brood might come up with!<br /> <br /> <br /> As other players have mentioned above, the New World of Darkness is not about having supernatural powers, it's a game about personal horror. You need to envision yourself in your character's situation and decide how they might react to finding out monsters are real, and they've become one against their will. Your character is clinically dead, they subsist on the blood of the living, and the touch of sunlight causes them to burst into flames.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but there's a centuries old, archaic monarchy in place who expects him to abide by their rules over night, or else they will send a hit squad to kill him for disturbing the peace. And there are multiple political factions, all of whom want to use him like a pawn to further their own goals that they've been planning decades before he was even born.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>HOW does a 16 year old boy raised in modern society respond to this?</i></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-23-2016, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:07:25-07:00","id":956320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956304#post956304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what I don't understand is so many VtR fans, unwillingness to facilitate style, and (when balanced) mechanical changes to reinforce unique character ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>What I don't understand is how common it is for people to come here asking if their concept fits the setting/rules and then getting defensive and refusing to budge when people say &quot;no, no it isn't, but here's how you can adjust it so that it does fit.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's remarkably common, but if all you wanted was validation, it sounds like your ST was already willing to work with you. You don't need us, and it's kind of misleading to ask &quot;am I being too creative?&quot; when you already have it set in your mind that your concept is fine for you and your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:08:18-07:00","id":956321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956315#post956315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest, your creativity is a little bit confusing. The first part of your character description makes it seem like he hates being a vampire and tries to keep in touch with his humanity, only for the next part to reveal he's specifically trained himself to sprout tentacles that ensnare and drink people. How did he develop this ability, why does he seem okay with using it if he hates feeding on people?<br /> <br /> If your argument is that it makes it easier to feed, you should know that the Nosferatu have a reputation for being physical power houses. If something goes wrong on the stealth tactic, the Nosferatu is quite capable of making an improvised exit via smashing through a wall.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I were the ST, I would definitely say that creating tentacles with mouths on them classifies as a Humanity breach. Any vampire who's willing to learn that ability would not be able to function at the level you're planning to use. In fact, it sounds like something that Belial's Brood might come up with!<br /> <br /> <br /> As other players have mentioned above, the New World of Darkness is not about having supernatural powers, it's a game about personal horror. You need to envision yourself in your character's situation and decide how they might react to finding out monsters are real, and they've become one against their will. Your character is clinically dead, they subsist on the blood of the living, and the touch of sunlight causes them to burst into flames.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but there's a centuries old, archaic monarchy in place who expects him to abide by their rules over night, or else they will send a hit squad to kill him for disturbing the peace. And there are multiple political factions, all of whom want to use him like a pawn to further their own goals that they've been planning decades before he was even born.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>HOW does a 16 year old boy raised in modern society respond to this?</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You are confusing the player with the character. The character is making the jarring realization that he is a monster. He doesn't learn this tentical maw power, its just a part of his body that horrifies him. He wants to drain people for their blood, this makes him feel guilty and ashamed. He is forced into conflict and made to use his powers. Over the campaign, he will slowly accept his nature, while still holding on to some of his ideals. Pretty much none of this is what HE wants, its what I want as a player to happen to him, and I designed the character with this in mind. To me, this sounds like I am trying to tell a story about personal horror.<br /> <br /> As for using superpowers to fight. If this game was not intended to facilitate vampires using badass powers to fight each other on occasion, then they should not have made a game with tons of cool superpowers to fight with. My Storyteller tends to like to put cool fights in his game, although they only make up about 20% of the play time. If I want to make a character that is good at fighting, I am actually at a disadvantage for most of the game, which will be spend in social conflict and investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:14:40-07:00","id":956326,"title":"","content":"Maina, I am not sure how much more I can budge than I already have. I asked for advice to see if it was balanced, you all have made it clear its not, so I abandoned the idea. My annoyance is not with people that are trying to help me balance it. The additude of some the post annoy me. It's like they think its a bad idea to make any changes.<br /> <br /> Also, why can't I quote you. I can quote everyone else, its weird...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-23-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:20:29-07:00","id":956331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956307#post956307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for me and my group - a lot of our past struggles over style have been trying to break away from what we call 'Vampions' - the trap that people seem to fall into by playing Requiem more like a 'Vampires w/ Superpowers' game over a one about the struggle of personal horror and immortal politics. This merit more reminds me of a comic character - like Venom, for example - than the NPCs and PCs I usually make.<br /> <br /> I routinely work with players to come up with custom mechanics and bonuses, but I like them to fit the setting I have in place. I'm less likely to approve something that clashes with the existing or intended style. I'm more likely to do so in a new startup game, but I'd want to really talk about the style clash and hopefully work that style into the world building at the outset to eliminate the clash altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that, although it seems like one of the best ways to do that is to take out all physical diciplines. If you have things like Vigor, Celerity, or Protean players would feel incentivised to use them like superpower, since that is essentually what they are. I could see some merit in a group of players just playing traditional blood sucking vamps without the ability to be much more powerful than humans, only using occasional mental powers. Maybe they could cost 2 Vitae instead of one per use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:25:37-07:00","id":956332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956321#post956321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Storyteller tends to like to put cool fights in his game, although they only make up about 20% of the play time. If I want to make a character that is good at fighting, I am actually at a disadvantage for most of the game, which will be spend in social conflict and investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not true. It's very easy to make character competent at combat while not being behind at other things. The thing about CofD is that it's easy to hit certain benchmark of good for low investment, and then you start getting diminishing returns on your investment while trying to pump that more and more. You can make your character good at combat by either putting a lot of skill dots in it, OR getting a good fighting style, OR getting a strong combat discipline. You don't need all of them to be effective. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:31:40-07:00","id":956336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956332#post956332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually not true. It's very easy to make character competent at combat while not being behind at other things. The thing about CofD is that it's easy to hit certain benchmark of good for low investment, and then you start getting diminishing returns on your investment while trying to pump that more and more. You can make your character good at combat by either putting a lot of skill dots in it, OR getting a good fighting style, OR getting a strong combat discipline. You don't need all of them to be effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the things we liked about the game, although in my characters case, he is a kid that will probably want an authority figure that he can cling to as surregate parental figure. With his underdeveloped emotional maturity, life experance, and lack of mental dicipline or great social skills, I wouldn't be supprised to see him get Diablerized or get a blood bond early on in the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:49:31-07:00","id":956344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956321#post956321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are confusing the player with the character. The character is making the jarring realization that he is a monster. He doesn't learn this tentical maw power, its just a part of his body that horrifies him. He wants to drain people for their blood, this makes him feel guilty and ashamed. He is forced into conflict and made to use his powers. Over the campaign, he will slowly accept his nature, while still holding on to some of his ideals. Pretty much none of this is what HE wants, its what I want as a player to happen to him, and I designed the character with this in mind. To me, this sounds like I am trying to tell a story about personal horror.<br /> <br /> As for using superpowers to fight. If this game was not intended to facilitate vampires using badass powers to fight each other on occasion, then they should not have made a game with tons of cool superpowers to fight with. My Storyteller tends to like to put cool fights in his game, although they only make up about 20% of the play time. If I want to make a character that is good at fighting, I am actually at a disadvantage for most of the game, which will be spend in social conflict and investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, it sounded like you were planning to keep him as a good guy from the first explanation of him.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the game having so many super powers, that's because World of Darkness does not focus on one particular Vampire mythos. It includes <i>all vampire mythos</i> rolled into one. That was the whole point of having multiple clans and bloodlines, because different cultures have different versions of what a vampire is supposed to be like. Some legends claim they can shapeshift, while others say they have superhuman prowess, or the ability to hypnotize you with a glare, or they're irresistibly charismatic. In some cultures, vampires aren't even reanimated corpses, but rather they're disembodied spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> The original world of darkness with Masquerade did focus more on the whole supernatural battle scenario. As it was described to me, you'd have vampires engaging in Kill Bill style katana fights on top of sky scrapers. The New World of Darkness broke away from that in order to focus more on the subtle, underlying themes of horror. You were raised as a human, now you're something that preys on them. How you learn to cope with that is up for you and the Story Teller to explore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Each of the 5 clans in Requiem is an archetype representation of the popular vampire story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Venture</b> - Powerful and aristocratic. The kind of vampire demonstrated in the tales of Dracula, or Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - Savage and predatory. The kind of vampires that Fright Night demonstrates.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> - Hideous and terrifying. The kind of vampires represented in old country folk lore.<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva</b> - Seductive and graceful. The kind of vampires represented in just about any modern media.<br /> <br /> <b>Mekhet</b> - Mysterious and cunning. The kind of vampire that conspiracy theorists go on about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are just the basic archetypes. The Bloodlines are a means of applying cultural history to them in order to provide more depth to their functionality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also, while it is technically possible for a Vampire to learn every Discipline, the chances of them actually doing so are extremely slim. Vampires don't just spontaneously acquire new powers, they need to be trained. Usually, this training comes from their sire. And most Vampires cap out after learning 5 Disciplines because of the stress of keeping up with all that training. That means that, at most, the average vampire would only exhibit 5 power sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-23-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:27:00-07:00","id":956445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956331#post956331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand that, although it seems like one of the best ways to do that is to take out all physical diciplines. If you have things like Vigor, Celerity, or Protean players would feel incentivised to use them like superpower, since that is essentually what they are. I could see some merit in a group of players just playing traditional blood sucking vamps without the ability to be much more powerful than humans, only using occasional mental powers. Maybe they could cost 2 Vitae instead of one per use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less the power mechanics, but more how they're utilized. As you point out, a character focused in combat abilities might get left behind in the political/social scene. If players are okay with that and fully aware there will be times they are taking a back seat - that actually helps a lot from my perspective. Sometimes, though, players <i>say </i>that - and then get bored or restless and so want to transition those physical powers into the social sphere so they can get back into the spotlight.<br /> <br /> The thing is - that <i>can </i>work too, but it takes a little more nuance/skill to pull it off. The Nosferatu Sheriff shaking your hand with an iron vice-grip as you agree to support his efforts in covering the Masquerade reminds you exactly what he can do if you fail. The Gangrel harpy whispering to you off in the corner who trails the tip of her claw along your earlobe reminds you that more than her words have edges.<br /> <br /> Instead, when it goes wrong, you have physical players punching their way to social 'success' and it can be very disruptive. The social characters feel like they're taking a backseat in their own realm, or they need to now get their own physical capabilities to compete. Basically it can be an infectious playstyle. It's really hard to teach a class or appreciate the fine details of sculpting, for example, when there's a bull in the studio wrecking things. Everyone kinda has to address the bull. Softer political scenes can be like that too.<br /> <br /> But I'll admit, purely physical disciplines will usually rank pretty low on my wishlists for the PCs I make.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion, and good luck with your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:56:20-07:00","id":956470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956344#post956344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, it sounded like you were planning to keep him as a good guy from the first explanation of him.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the game having so many super powers, that's because World of Darkness does not focus on one particular Vampire mythos. It includes <i>all vampire mythos</i> rolled into one. That was the whole point of having multiple clans and bloodlines, because different cultures have different versions of what a vampire is supposed to be like. Some legends claim they can shapeshift, while others say they have superhuman prowess, or the ability to hypnotize you with a glare, or they're irresistibly charismatic. In some cultures, vampires aren't even reanimated corpses, but rather they're disembodied spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> The original world of darkness with Masquerade did focus more on the whole supernatural battle scenario. As it was described to me, you'd have vampires engaging in Kill Bill style katana fights on top of sky scrapers. The New World of Darkness broke away from that in order to focus more on the subtle, underlying themes of horror. You were raised as a human, now you're something that preys on them. How you learn to cope with that is up for you and the Story Teller to explore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Each of the 5 clans in Requiem is an archetype representation of the popular vampire story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Venture</b> - Powerful and aristocratic. The kind of vampire demonstrated in the tales of Dracula, or Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - Savage and predatory. The kind of vampires that Fright Night demonstrates.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> - Hideous and terrifying. The kind of vampires represented in old country folk lore.<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva</b> - Seductive and graceful. The kind of vampires represented in just about any modern media.<br /> <br /> <b>Mekhet</b> - Mysterious and cunning. The kind of vampire that conspiracy theorists go on about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are just the basic archetypes. The Bloodlines are a means of applying cultural history to them in order to provide more depth to their functionality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also, while it is technically possible for a Vampire to learn every Discipline, the chances of them actually doing so are extremely slim. Vampires don't just spontaneously acquire new powers, they need to be trained. Usually, this training comes from their sire. And most Vampires cap out after learning 5 Disciplines because of the stress of keeping up with all that training. That means that, at most, the average vampire would only exhibit 5 power sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I never really thought of disciplines as something you would actually need training for. I thought that they were powers, either natural to the vampire, or given by blood, and that the dot represents getting stronger as you get more Vitae. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, Mekhet aren't really a vampire from folk lore or pop culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:46:07-07:00","id":956497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956470#post956470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I never really thought of disciplines as something you would actually need training for. I thought that they were powers, either natural to the vampire, or given by blood, and that the dot represents getting stronger as you get more Vitae.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, Mekhet aren't really a vampire from folk lore or pop culture.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, it's in their name &quot;Disciplines.&quot; As in, it's an acquired skill.<br /> <br /> Any vampire is capable of learning any Discipline, but it requires a conscious effort in order to do so. As I said, this training usually comes from the vampire's own sire, which is why at least 2 of your starting Disciplines must be clan related. Think of it as the parental vampire passing their skills down to their descendants.<br /> <br /> Disciplines that aren't part of the clan's natural affinity require the vampire to either find a teacher someplace else, or develop it through trial and error. That's why it requires more experience to master them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The signature Disciplines of each clan / bloodline are exactly that, their signature ability. They're the ones who invented it, they perfected it, and they keep its power a closely guarded secret. They can be convinced to teach others what they know, but this knowledge does not come freely. Any vampire who wants to learn it is going to have to earn that privilege, which your character can not possibly have done if he was only embraced yesterday.<br /> <br /> <br /> Protean was developed through the Gangrel's deep connection with the natural environment. They've weaponized their Beast, turning it into a tool for satisfying their needs. Most vampires are too busy trying to suppress their Beast to think about harmonizing with it. So learning how to shapeshift for a non-Gangrel is not a subject to be treated lightly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I should have said that the Mekhet represent the occult mysticism that surrounds the undead. If the Ventrue are the public face of leadership, the Mekhet are the shadowy puppet masters who watch from afar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-23-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:27:18-07:00","id":956549,"title":"","content":"Not to rehash the argument from another thread, but there is book evidence that Disciplines do manifest naturally and exist in the blood, independent of training. Arguments could be made either way, but I think they're far more innate than you're presenting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:48:45-07:00","id":956627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956549#post956549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to rehash the argument from another thread, but there is book evidence that Disciplines do manifest naturally and exist in the blood, independent of training. Arguments could be made either way, but I think they're far more innate than you're presenting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the fact that you must consume some Vitae from another vampire to learn a discipline. I know that there is an element of personal experiance, and skill involved, but it certianly sounds like its primarily a power to me. Not to mention, a vampire can start with up to 3 disciplines from the moment they are embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:56:51-07:00","id":956631,"title":"","content":"Here is another question for you folks, since we have beaten the last horse as much as we can. Does anyone have any advice for playing a kidpire? His personality is similar to Carl Grimes from The Walking Dead. His name is Caleb Xaine (very typical for a vampire I know) I intend for him to be a helpful follower, who stays out of the adults way, but knows when to jump in and help, I also want to age him down a bit to play up the child vampire story, say 14 or 15 so he will be old enough to grasp personal responsibility. I have ditched the Gangrel and Nosferatu idea, and all related powers. He will be a Mekhet and spy for our group, if we turn out to need one. One importaint thing about this game is that all spontainiously sireless vampires have a rank three blood sympathy with each other at the start, presumably its importaint to the story. Also how should I feed? I was gonna keep his strength at 1 dot, since he is small, so violent feeding might be a bad idea, but I also doubt a 14 year old could seduce anyone. Also gave him the small framed merit, its it worth having Obfuscate and small frame, or is it a waste?<br /> <br /> Oh, and he will get all Obfuscate, Celerity, and Auspex, or maybe two dots of Auspex, and one dot of Celerity, I haven't decided yet. Auspex doesn't seem that great until four, so I might need a head start on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-23-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:58:41-07:00","id":956633,"title":"","content":"Only to learn clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Blood &amp; Smoke p125, 'Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred only display the Disciplines of their Clan.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:21:27-07:00","id":956642,"title":"","content":"You might want to look at the Children's Crusade under the Broken Covenants section. I'm not sure that 14 would be young enough to count, but there might be some older or more scholarly vampires uncomfortable with the concept.<br /> <br /> Still, it might give basic ideas for how youth affects vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:22:58-07:00","id":956643,"title":"","content":"I make a mistake in the last post, we don't get blood bonds, we get 3 blood sympathy. I edited it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-23-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:56:22-07:00","id":956657,"title":"","content":"First, watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ICp4g9p_rgo\" target=\"_blank\">Let the Right One In</a>.<br /> <br /> I would personally play up the helplessness aspect in feeding and attempt to have the other characters take on that responsibility for you, bringing you back victims, maybe animals, maybe people. All that in exchange for your sneak / spy abilities on behalf of the group. I like the small frame combo, but it's really up to your ST how useful it will be. Ask them if there would be an advantage in it for you or not.<br /> <br /> If the other character won't play ball and help you feed, I'd go the sandman route, which involves sneaking into domiciles to feed on people who are sleeping. Takes advantage of those natural Obs/small qualities if you go that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:00:20-07:00","id":956659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956631#post956631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how should I feed? I was gonna keep his strength at 1 dot, since he is small, so violent feeding might be a bad idea, but I also doubt a 14 year old could seduce anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could seduce other 14 year olds. Or at least get intimate access to them at night. They're young enough to feast on animal blood so you could have access to a pound. In previous games of ours such vampires have fed through 'adopted' parents or other guardians, reinforcing loyalty through blood bondage, or just been part of a crowd of similarly aged kids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also gave him the small framed merit, its it worth having Obfuscate and small frame, or is it a waste? </div> </div> </div>The small-framed merit makes sense for a child like that, I'd probably have required it if you wanted to play someone that young. But its not really related to Obfuscate, which effectively turns you invisible, albeit via psychic cloaking. It would offer some bonuses to more mundane stealth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Auspex doesn't seem that great until four, so I might need a head start on it. </div> </div> </div>1 and 2 are great, especially if you're meant to be a spy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:00:25-07:00","id":956660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956631#post956631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another question for you folks, since we have beaten the last horse as much as we can. Does anyone have any advice for playing a kidpire? His personality is similar to Carl Grimes from The Walking Dead. His name is Caleb Xaine (very typical for a vampire I know) I intend for him to be a helpful follower, who stays out of the adults way, but knows when to jump in and help, I also want to age him down a bit to play up the child vampire story, say 14 or 15 so he will be old enough to grasp personal responsibility. I have ditched the Gangrel and Nosferatu idea, and all related powers. He will be a Mekhet and spy for our group, if we turn out to need one. One importaint thing about this game is that all spontainiously sireless vampires have a rank three blood sympathy with each other at the start, presumably its importaint to the story. Also how should I feed? I was gonna keep his strength at 1 dot, since he is small, so violent feeding might be a bad idea, but I also doubt a 14 year old could seduce anyone. Also gave him the small framed merit, its it worth having Obfuscate and small frame, or is it a waste?<br /> <br /> Oh, and he will get all Obfuscate, Celerity, and Auspex, or maybe two dots of Auspex, and one dot of Celerity, I haven't decided yet. Auspex doesn't seem that great until four, so I might need a head start on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Youd' be surprised, there's a lot of perverts out there. And World of Darkness is supposed to be a darker version of our world, which means its even more likely he'll come across somebody who's into that stuff.<br /> <br /> The major problem with playing a vampire kid (in my opinion anyways) is the social complications that would create. You're a child, walking around in the middle of the night without adult supervision unless you're with a coterie who you can pass off as your legal guardians. Most night clubs and bars aren't going to let you enter to scope out a blood donor, and money is going to be very difficult to come by, thanks to child labor laws.<br /> <br /> Simply put, there's a bunch of crap vampires have to deal with that would be extremely difficult for a child to manage properly, which is why embracing children is commonly seen as taboo in vampire society.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for his strength matching his size, that's not really a big issue for vampires. They're supernatural beings, after all.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about his base strength, then yeah, that would make sense. But you could use Vigor to enhance him beyond most adults.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would recommend going with a high Auspex starting out, and explain it in story as him learning to keep alert for opportunities and threats, since he has a harder time surviving than full grown vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:08:22-07:00","id":956666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956660#post956660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major problem with playing a vampire kid (in my opinion anyways) is the social complications that would create. You're a child, walking around in the middle of the night without adult supervision unless you're with a coterie who you can pass off as your legal guardians. Most night clubs and bars aren't going to let you enter to scope out a blood donor, and money is going to be very difficult to come by, thanks to child labor laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately they have access to Obfuscate, which covers this from the first dot, and for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:45:06-07:00","id":956681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956666#post956666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately they have access to Obfuscate, which covers this from the first dot, and for free.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought the first dot just let you obscure small, easy to carry objects from detection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:49:47-07:00","id":956684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956681#post956681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the first dot just let you obscure small, easy to carry objects from detection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Providing we're talking about second edition, that's the second dot. First is face in a crowd, which makes people overlook you as if you're just one of the crowd.<br /> <br /> Without Obfuscate, a kid character would have to deal with all the problems you've mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:52:13-07:00","id":956688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956684#post956684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Providing we're talking about second edition, that's the second dot. First is face in a crowd, which makes people overlook you as if you're just one of the crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, okay then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:35:30-07:00","id":956702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/948011-my-questionable-vampire-character?p=956657#post956657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ICp4g9p_rgo\" target=\"_blank\">Let the Right One In</a>.<br /> <br /> I would personally play up the helplessness aspect in feeding and attempt to have the other characters take on that responsibility for you, bringing you back victims, maybe animals, maybe people. All that in exchange for your sneak / spy abilities on behalf of the group. I like the small frame combo, but it's really up to your ST how useful it will be. Ask them if there would be an advantage in it for you or not.<br /> <br /> If the other character won't play ball and help you feed, I'd go the sandman route, which involves sneaking into domiciles to feed on people who are sleeping. Takes advantage of those natural Obs/small qualities if you go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE Let The Right One In. It is not really the same for my character as he is older, but I saw both versions of the movie and read the book.<br /> <br /> Funny story, my Storyteller also watched both versions of the movie, and read the book, and his response after all of that was &quot;hmmm, didn't care for it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:35:30-07:00","id":971808,"title":"","content":"Hey everybody. I just want to thank everyone for sharing their ideas last month and helping me make my first vampire the requiem character. After all the discussions this is what I came up with. I wrote this for my Storyteller, so not everything will nessessarly make sense out of context. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1c7M83o8Xi2UT7oc-h6Z8ToxALDR2l4bLcA91jSBH2Og/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...91jSBH2Og/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 09-18-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:28:41-07:00","id":972030,"title":"","content":"Heh, having their epitaph as a header is a nice touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:02:59-07:00","id":972087,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:44:08-07:00","id":972134,"title":"","content":"I just saw this. Glad it worked out for you. I was surprised nobody thought of squid tentacles. You could justify claws and prehensile tail. As squid are aquatic creatures and I'm not a 